  "details": "Currently, when editing your bio and it exceeds the character amount, you have to restart, losing all that bio you just typed. This is the same when updating status. Even worse, you lose *all* edited profile sections when on eof those go past their set limit.\n\nIt would be really, and i mean *really* cool and highly appreciated if you could see how many characters you have left in your bio or status.\n\nAnother Suggestion for this topic is keeping your editing drafts instead of discarding your edits when a section is too long. The amount of times I've raged about losing what I've typed is immense.\n\nI really wish something like that would happen, as i see many websites preventing you from hitting 'continue' if a string is invalid in any way it might be. And I might be wrong about this, but didn't we used to have a char diaplay on the website? Or am i wrong on that?",
